 "asked_at": "2026-10-17T21:28+08:00",
 "answer": "Yes, the haze is bad in KL today (17 Oct). Readings are in the \"unhealthy\" range, though not yet \"very unhealthy\".\n\n**Latest readings (as of 9.30am):**\n- In Kuala Lumpur, Cheras recorded an API of 162 and Batu Muda 159, while Putrajaya also registered 162.\n- Nearby areas are similar. Petaling Jaya and Shah Alam recorded 169 each, and Klang 171.\n- Nationwide, 24 areas recorded unhealthy air quality, with Pasir Gudang, Johor, highest at 196.\n\n**What the numbers mean:** 0–50 is good, 51–100 moderate, 101–200 unhealthy, 201–300 very unhealthy, and above 300 hazardous. KL is in the middle of the \"unhealthy\" band.\n\n**Trend:** The haze has lasted several days. Earlier this week, 34 areas recorded unhealthy readings as of 5 pm, with Klang the highest at 195. Today's morning count is lower, but the situation is still serious. Readings change through the day, so check again later.\n\n**Precautions:**\n- Limit strenuous outdoor activity. This matters most for children, older people, and anyone with asthma, heart or lung conditions.\n- Wear a well-fitted N95 mask if you have to go out.\n- Keep windows closed and use an air purifier or air-conditioning if you have one.\n- Under the school procedures, outdoor activities are postponed when the API goes above 100.\n\nFor live figures, check the Department of Environment's MyAQI site or app (APIMS).",
